exports[`spine full axis matrix (16 representative cells) > baseline-frontier-astronomy: stable spine + body[0] structural fields 1`] = `
{
  "body0": "Reduced to observables, the driver is this — prices around Atlas-Bridge I have tripled since the last safe-window season. In the record, Tau Reticuli Cohort appears as claimant and Tau Reticuli Service as incumbent; the field data is less tidy. One term in the system does not close: The compact between Tau Reticuli Cohort and Tau Reticuli Service fractured in the first ephemeris pass. Three bodies define this problem: the failed terraforming biosphere, Catalog Authority, and Tau Reticuli Trust, which absorbs the perturbations. The boundary condition nobody can renegotiate: the insurers have quietly reclassified everything near Failed terraforming biosphere. Rebuild crews work the damaged ring under floodlights, around the clock, without press. The medical chirality stock versus Atlas-Bridge VII Station 18 is the headline; the secular decline in conditions at Atlas-Bridge II Station 88 is the data. Every model of the dispute shares one input: redundancy was cut three budgets ago and never restored. Salvage from the worst of it is still being sold with the serial numbers filed off. The dependency coefficient linking Atlas-Bridge II Station 88 to Medical chirality stock has grown every audit cycle since records began.",
  "spineEdgeType": "CONTESTS",
  "spineObjectKind": "namedFaction",
  "spineSubjectKind": "namedFaction",
  "spineSummary": "The compact between Tau Reticuli Cohort and Tau Reticuli Service broke in the first ephemeris pass, the defining variable in this system is institutional: the two of them cannot agree on who certifies the numbers.",
  "spineVisibility": "contested",
}
`;

exports[`spine full axis matrix (16 representative cells) > baseline-frontier-balanced: stable spine + body[0] structural fields 1`] = `
{
  "body0": "New storage capacity gets built at triple redundancy and nobody calls it overreaction. The metric shear condensates presses, Mothallah Corridor-631 III Station 71 holds, and Mothallah Corridor-631 II Charter pays for both: wages frozen until someone blinks. Strip away the filings and the cause is plain — the supply contract renews on terms nobody has seen yet. Alarm drills stopped being announced; nobody needed the announcements. The principals are the debt-fleet anchor graveyard and Mothallah Corridor-631 V; the casualty ledger, so far, is kept at Old navy depot. The pressure underneath is simple: evacuation drills have gone from annual to weekly without an announcement. The metric shear condensates wants first claim on the next harvest window; Mothallah Corridor-631 V - Moon I Claim guards the margin that keeps the lights on; Mothallah Corridor-631 II Charter gets a clinic that treats casualties from either camp and bills neither. The dispute runs at a simmer, and simmers out here have a way of finding fuel. One fact would reshuffle every position if it surfaced: the plague is industrial poisoning. The joint maintenance schedule still runs, but each side sends its own inspector to watch the other's. The ground lease under Old navy depot predates half the law that governs Mothallah Corridor-631 V. There, There is no second source for Metric shear condensates, and everyone at Mothallah Corridor-631 II Charter has done the math.",
  "spineEdgeType": "DEPENDS_ON",
  "spineObjectKind": "guResource",
  "spineSubjectKind": "settlement",
  "spineSummary": "Everything else about this system is negotiable; Mothallah Corridor-631 III Station 71's need for Metric shear condensates is not.",
  "spineVisibility": "public",
}
`;

exports[`spine full axis matrix (16 representative cells) > baseline-frontier-cinematic: stable spine + body[0] structural fields 1`] = `
{
  "body0": "The war is on, whatever the bulletins call it. The fight belongs to the first-wave ghost colony and Ceibo's Breach IV; the bleeding is done at Ceibo's Breach IV Dome. Every shift change, someone repaints the boundary line around the chiral volatile reservoirs a hand-width farther out. Legal filings over Ceibo's Breach IV Dome arrive faster than the courts can docket them. Brothers of Choir sharpens, Pale Saint Pact braces, and Carrion Wake learns to sleep in a pressure suit. The fuse is lit at both ends and burning politely. Cargo manifests between the two camps now travel with notarized seals nobody used to bother with. When Carrion Wake and Vow-Breaker Wake finally close, it will be Brothers of Choir standing between them, holding the freight surcharge that lands on them no matter who wins. For now the knives stay sheathed, and the sheaths get oiled nightly. Ceibo's Breach IV was here first, and everything about Ceibo's Breach IV Dome apologizes for it.",
